The graph shows the balance owing on a $\$45\,000$ loan under two different monthly repayments.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=122,ymin=0,ymax=50000,xtick={0,20,40,60,80,100,120},ytick={0,10000,20000,30000,40000},grid=both,samples=80,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Months},ylabel={Balance owing (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:110.4]{67500 - 22500*exp(x*ln(1.01))} node[pos=0.62,above right,blue,font=\small]{$\$675$ per month};
\addplot[thick,red,dashed,domain=0:40.7]{135000 - 90000*exp(x*ln(1.01))} node[pos=0.786,above right,red,font=\small]{$\$1350$ per month};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
To the nearest $10$ months, how long does the loan take at $\$1350$ per month?
